<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Checksum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A checksum/hash over a byte range. Each END of the range is stated independently: a field reference (coversFromField/coversToField) or a HEL expression yielding a byte offset (coversFromExpression/coversToExpression). The two ends may use different mechanisms -- a checksum covering everything from a named header field to a length carried elsewhere needs exactly that. Note the boundary convention differs by mechanism, because each follows what its inputs naturally give: the field form runs from the FIRST byte of coversFromField to the LAST byte of coversToField (inclusive), while the expression form is the half-open [start,end) that the two offsets delimit."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Checksum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ChecksumAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An identifier for an integrity-check algorithm; a profile must resolve algorithm variants and parameters unambiguously."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ChecksumAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ChecksumShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:checksumAlgorithm, bddo:coversExpression, bddo:coversFromExpression, bddo:coversFromField, bddo:coversToExpression, bddo:coversToField. bddo:checksumAlgorithm is one of the named algorithms or a bddo:CustomCrc."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ChecksumShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Checksum; objects of bddo:checksum Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ChecksumShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Checksum Shape"@en .
