<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ConditionalEndiannessShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#CustomCrc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A CRC stated by its Rocksoft-model parameters rather than named: bddo:crcWidth (8..64 bits), bddo:crcPolynomial, bddo:crcInit, bddo:crcReflectIn, bddo:crcReflectOut and bddo:crcXorOut, all six required. Used as the value of bddo:checksumAlgorithm for a CRC that no named algorithm identifies."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#CustomCrc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#CustomCrcShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:crcInit, bddo:crcPolynomial, bddo:crcReflectIn, bddo:crcReflectOut, bddo:crcWidth, bddo:crcXorOut. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcInit. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcPolynomial. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcReflectIn. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcReflectOut. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcWidth, an integer from 8 to 64. A bddo:CustomCrc states exactly one bddo:crcXorOut. {?p} {?v} does not fit a {?w}-bit CRC: it must be below 2^{?w}."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#CustomCrcShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:CustomCrc Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
