<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecords> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Struct whose children are located by delimiter position rather than byte offset: a byte run split into records by recordDelimiter, each record optionally split into values by fieldDelimiter."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecords> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:commentPrefix, bddo:escapeChar, bddo:fieldDelimiter, bddo:hasField, bddo:keyValueSeparator, bddo:quoteChar, bddo:recordDelimiter, bddo:skipRecords, bddo:trimWhitespace, bddo:whitespaceSeparated. A bddo:DelimitedRecords must declare at least one field."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DelimitedRecords Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delimited Records Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "DelimitedRecords whose records are rows with a fixed column sequence. The hasField list gives the columns in order; the row structure repeats until the byte run is exhausted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:fieldDelimiter, bddo:key, bddo:keyValueSeparator, bddo:whitespaceSeparated. bddo:key applies to a field of a KeyValueHeader; a DelimitedTable's columns are located by position. bddo:keyValueSeparator applies to a KeyValueHeader, not a DelimitedTable."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DelimitedTable Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delimited Table Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DelimitedTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DerivedFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Derived Field. A bddo:valueFromExpression (derived) field must not also declare a byte-consuming mechanism (dataType, hasConditionalDataType, size*, terminator, bitLength, atOffset* or enumeration)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DerivedFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DerivedFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Derived Field Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DerivedFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DisjointKindsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A node is at most one of bddo:Struct, bddo:Field and bddo:DataType (subclasses included), as the owl:AllDisjointClasses axiom states."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DisjointKindsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DataType, bddo:Field, bddo:Struct Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One key-to-type association contributed to a dispatch table; keys are unique within a table across all contributing graphs."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArmShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:armDataType, bddo:armKey, bddo:armTable. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArmShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DispatchArm; subjects using bddo:armDataType, bddo:armKey, bddo:armTable Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArmShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispatch Arm Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchArmShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchKeyUniquenessShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Dispatch Key Uniqueness. Two DispatchArms of one DispatchTable declare the same armKey."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchKeyUniquenessShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DispatchTable Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchKeyUniquenessShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispatch Key Uniqueness Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchKeyUniquenessShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A keyed, open selection of a field's effective type: the dispatch key is matched by equality against the keys of arms that any importing description may contribute."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:dispatchDefault, bddo:dispatchOnExpression, bddo:dispatchOnField. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DispatchTable Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dispatch Table Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#DispatchTableShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Encoding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A character encoding used to convert a sequence of bytes to text."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Encoding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Endianness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The order in which the bytes of a multi-byte value contribute to its significance."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Endianness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One arm of a hasConditionalEndianness list: a HEL condition and the byte order it selects."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRule> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:condition, bddo:ruleEndianness. bddo:ruleEndianness must be bddo:BigEndian or bddo:LittleEndian."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:EndiannessRule Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Endianness Rule Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EndiannessRuleShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One association between a raw enumeration value and the semantic symbol it denotes."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValue> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:enumRawValue, bddo:enumSymbol. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:EnumValue Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Enum Value Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Enumeration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A mapping from raw parsed values, or bit masks when flags are enabled, to semantic symbol IRIs."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Enumeration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumerationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:enumIsFlags, bddo:hasEnumValue. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumerationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Enumeration Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumerationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Enumeration Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#EnumerationShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Field> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A single element within a Struct: a value, a bit slice, or an array."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Field> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldOffsetShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Field Offset. A bddo:Field must use at most one offset mechanism."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldOffsetShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldOffsetShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Field Offset Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldOffsetShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldRepetitionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Field Repetition. A bddo:Field must use at most one repetition mechanism."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldRepetitionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldRepetitionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Field Repetition Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldRepetitionShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:alignment, bddo:atOffset, bddo:atOffsetFromExpression, bddo:atOffsetFromField, bddo:bitLength, bddo:checksum, bddo:dataType, bddo:encoding, bddo:enumeration, bddo:hasConditionalDataType, bddo:hasDispatchTable, bddo:isPresentIf, bddo:offsetBase, bddo:rootKeyFromField, bddo:seekScope, bddo:separatedBy, bddo:size, bddo:sizeFromExpression, bddo:sizeFromField, bddo:sizeToEndOfStream, bddo:terminator, bddo:trimNull, bddo:validIf, bddo:valueFromExpression. Every member of a hasConditionalDataType list must be a bddo:DataTypeRule."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Field Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Field Sizing. A bddo:Field must use at most one sizing/termination mechanism."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Field Sizing Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FieldSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FloatParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The parameter accepts a HEL Float; an Integer argument is converted to the Float of the same value."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#FloatParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:hasGrouping, bddo:pathSeparator. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:DelimitedRecords Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grouped Records Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupedRecordsShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupingStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Which of the three ways a text format marks a nested group."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#GroupingStyle> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#IntegerParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The parameter accepts a HEL Integer."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#IntegerParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#IntegerValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Integer value. Its constraints below specify the permitted values and combinations."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#IntegerValueShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: No automatic target; applied only when another shape references it or a caller explicitly selects it. Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyPathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:keyPath. bddo:keyPath locates a field inside nested groups, so its container must declare bddo:hasGrouping; without one the container is flat and the path addresses nothing."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyPathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyPathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Key Path Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyPathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeader> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "DelimitedRecords whose records are key/value pairs split by keyValueSeparator. Each expected key is a Field carrying bddo:key, or, with no bddo:key, named by its simple key (the local name of its IRI after the last '.'); record order is not significant."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeader> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeaderShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:key, bddo:keyPath, bddo:keyValueSeparator. A bddo:KeyValueHeader must declare bddo:keyValueSeparator. Every field of a bddo:KeyValueHeader declares at most one bddo:key (flat) or one bddo:keyPath (nested), never both; a field with neither is located by its simple key."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeaderShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:KeyValueHeader Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeaderShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Key Value Header Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#KeyValueHeaderShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bit order consuming the least significant remaining bit of each byte first."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LittleEndian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Byte order placing the least significant byte of a multi-byte value first."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LittleEndian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LittleEndian> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A named HEL value local to one Struct instance: a member of the struct's bddo:hasField list whose bddo:localExpression is evaluated when its position in the list is reached, in the struct's context. Later members, and the struct's own size, count, offset and presence expressions evaluated after it, read it by bare name or instance.<name>. It consumes no bytes, is not part of the parsed tree and is never lifted. Its name is the simple key of its IRI, as for a Field."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:localExpression. A bddo:LocalBinding is a member of a binary struct; {?container} is a delimited or tree container. A bddo:LocalBinding states exactly one bddo:localExpression."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:LocalBinding; subjects using bddo:localExpression Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Local Binding Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#LocalBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#MSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Bit order consuming the most significant remaining bit of each byte first."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#MSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#MSBFirst> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A prefix-to-IRI binding for the paths of an XML TreeDocument."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBinding> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:namespaceIRI, bddo:namespacePrefix. A namespace binding needs the IRI it binds to; a prefix alone names nothing. bddo:namespaceIRI must be an absolute IRI (it begins with a scheme)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:NamespaceBinding; subjects using bddo:namespaceIRI, bddo:namespacePrefix; objects of bddo:hasNamespaceBinding Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Namespace Binding Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NamespaceBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NodePathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:nodePath. This bddo:nodePath ({?p}) is not a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901): it must be empty or a sequence of /-prefixed reference tokens, with ~ only in ~0 or ~1. This bddo:nodePath ({?p}) is not an abbreviated XPath of child steps, optional [n] positions (n >= 1) and at most one final @attribute step. bddo:nodePath locates a node in a parsed tree, so every container of the field must be a bddo:TreeDocument ({?container} is not, or there is none)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NodePathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field; subjects using bddo:nodePath Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NodePathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Node Path Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NodePathShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NumericBaseShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:dataType, bddo:numericBase. bddo:numericBase applies only to a field whose bddo:dataType is bddo:asciiInteger. bddo:numericBase must be 8, 10 or 16."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NumericBaseShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using bddo:numericBase Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NumericBaseShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Numeric Base Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#NumericBaseShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#OffsetBase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The reference position against which an explicit field offset is resolved."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#OffsetBase> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Parameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "One formal parameter of a parameterised Struct, a member of its bddo:hasParameter list. Its name is the simple key of its IRI (the local name after the last '.'), as for a Field; HEL reads the value the caller supplied as param.<name>. A parameter consumes no bytes, is not a field of the parsed tree and is never lifted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Parameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:parameterType. bddo:parameterType is one of bddo:IntegerParameter, bddo:FloatParameter, bddo:StringParameter, bddo:BytesParameter and bddo:BooleanParameter."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Parameter; subjects using bddo:parameterType Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parameter Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The kind of HEL value a Parameter accepts: one of the five individuals below, one per HEL scalar value type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterisedStructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for rdf:type, bddo:hasParameter. Every member of a hasParameter list is a bddo:Parameter named by its IRI. bddo:hasParameter is declared on a bddo:Struct. bddo:hasParameter must point to a single rdf:List."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterisedStructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using bddo:hasParameter Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterisedStructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parameterised Struct Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ParameterisedStructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RangeDatatypeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:alignment, bddo:atOffset, bddo:atOffsetFromExpression, bddo:bitLength, bddo:bitWidth, bddo:commentPrefix, bddo:condition, bddo:coversExpression, bddo:coversFromExpression, bddo:coversToExpression, bddo:crcCheck, bddo:crcInit, bddo:crcPolynomial, bddo:crcReflectIn, bddo:crcReflectOut, bddo:crcWidth, bddo:crcXorOut, bddo:dispatchOnExpression, bddo:enumIsFlags, bddo:escapeChar, bddo:fieldDelimiter, bddo:groupCloseToken, bddo:groupOpenToken, bddo:isPresentIf, bddo:isSigned, bddo:key, bddo:keyIsCaseInsensitive, bddo:keyPath, bddo:keyValueSeparator, bddo:localExpression, bddo:namespaceIRI, bddo:namespacePrefix, bddo:nodePath, bddo:numericBase, bddo:pathSeparator, bddo:quoteChar, bddo:recordDelimiter, bddo:repeatCount, bddo:repeatCountFromExpression, bddo:repeatUntil, bddo:separatedBy, bddo:size, bddo:sizeFromExpression, bddo:sizeToEndOfStream, bddo:skipRecords, bddo:syncOnMarker, bddo:terminator, bddo:trimNull, bddo:trimWhitespace, bddo:validIf, bddo:valueFromExpression, bddo:whitespaceSeparated. bddo:alignment takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:atOffset takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:atOffsetFromExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:bitLength takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:bitWidth takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:commentPrefix takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:condition takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:coversExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:coversFromExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:coversToExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:crcCheck takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:crcInit takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:crcPolynomial takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:crcReflectIn takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:crcReflectOut takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:crcWidth takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:crcXorOut takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:dispatchOnExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:enumIsFlags takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:escapeChar takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:fieldDelimiter takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:groupCloseToken takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:groupOpenToken takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:isPresentIf takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:isSigned takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:key takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:keyIsCaseInsensitive takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:keyPath takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:keyValueSeparator takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:localExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:namespaceIRI takes an xsd:anyURI literal (rdfs:range xsd:anyURI). bddo:namespacePrefix takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:nodePath takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:numericBase takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:pathSeparator takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:quoteChar takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:recordDelimiter takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:repeatCount takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:repeatCountFromExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:repeatUntil takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:separatedBy takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:size takes a positive integer (rdfs:range xsd:positiveInteger). bddo:sizeFromExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:sizeToEndOfStream takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:skipRecords takes a non-negative integer (rdfs:range xsd:nonNegativeInteger). bddo:syncOnMarker takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:terminator takes an xsd:hexBinary literal (rdfs:range xsd:hexBinary). bddo:trimNull takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:trimWhitespace takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean). bddo:validIf takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:valueFromExpression takes an xsd:string literal (rdfs:range xsd:string). bddo:whitespaceSeparated takes an xsd:boolean literal (rdfs:range xsd:boolean)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RangeDatatypeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: subjects using bddo:alignment, bddo:atOffset, bddo:atOffsetFromExpression, bddo:bitLength, bddo:bitWidth, bddo:commentPrefix, bddo:condition, bddo:coversExpression, bddo:coversFromExpression, bddo:coversToExpression, bddo:crcCheck, bddo:crcInit, bddo:crcPolynomial, bddo:crcReflectIn, bddo:crcReflectOut, bddo:crcWidth, bddo:crcXorOut, bddo:dispatchOnExpression, bddo:enumIsFlags, bddo:escapeChar, bddo:fieldDelimiter, bddo:groupCloseToken, bddo:groupOpenToken, bddo:isPresentIf, bddo:isSigned, bddo:key, bddo:keyIsCaseInsensitive, bddo:keyPath, bddo:keyValueSeparator, bddo:localExpression, bddo:namespaceIRI, bddo:namespacePrefix, bddo:nodePath, bddo:numericBase, bddo:pathSeparator, bddo:quoteChar, bddo:recordDelimiter, bddo:repeatCount, bddo:repeatCountFromExpression, bddo:repeatUntil, bddo:separatedBy, bddo:size, bddo:sizeFromExpression, bddo:sizeToEndOfStream, bddo:skipRecords, bddo:syncOnMarker, bddo:terminator, bddo:trimNull, bddo:trimWhitespace, bddo:validIf, bddo:valueFromExpression, bddo:whitespaceSeparated Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGrouping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "How a DelimitedRecords container nests: which records open a group, which close it, and where the group's name comes from. A container without one is flat, which is what every DelimitedRecords was before nesting existed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGrouping> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGroupingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:groupCloseToken, bddo:groupOpenToken, bddo:groupingStyle. A bddo:RecordGrouping must name exactly one style: keyedGroup, valuedGroup or sectionHeaded."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGroupingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:RecordGrouping Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGroupingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Record Grouping Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#RecordGroupingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScope> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The reach of an offset-addressed read: the innermost bounded region, or the whole stream."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScope> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScopeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Seek Scope. bddo:seekScope is only meaningful on an offset-addressed Field (atOffset / atOffsetFromField / atOffsetFromExpression)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScopeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScopeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seek Scope Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#SeekScopeShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StringParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The parameter accepts a HEL String."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StringParameter> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Struct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An ordered sequence of fields; a container in a binary format."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#Struct> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:bitOrder, bddo:endianness, bddo:hasField, bddo:size, bddo:sizeFromExpression, bddo:sizeFromField, bddo:syncOnMarker. Every member of a Struct's hasField list must be a bddo:Field or a bddo:LocalBinding. bddo:hasField must point to a single rdf:List."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Struct Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Struct Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Struct Sizing. A bddo:Struct must use at most one sizing mechanism (size / sizeFromField / sizeFromExpression)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Struct Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Struct Sizing Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#StructSizingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Struct whose children are located by a path into a parsed node tree rather than by byte offset or delimiter. The byte run is handed to a parser for the declared syntax; each Field names the node supplying its value."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity. Its subclass links below are the asserted hierarchy, not merely similarity links."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocumentShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for bddo:atOffset, bddo:hasField, bddo:hasNamespaceBinding, bddo:key, bddo:keyPath, bddo:nodePath, bddo:treeSyntax. A bddo:TreeDocument must declare at least one field. A bddo:TreeDocument must declare exactly one bddo:treeSyntax: bddo:xml or bddo:json. Every field of a bddo:TreeDocument is located by exactly one bddo:nodePath, and not by a key, a key path or a byte offset. bddo:hasNamespaceBinding applies to an XML tree document; JSON Pointer has no namespace prefixes."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocumentShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:TreeDocument Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocumentShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tree Document Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeDocumentShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreePrefixBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Tree Prefix Binding. A bddo:nodePath of this XML tree document ({?p}) uses a prefix that no bddo:hasNamespaceBinding binds (only xml is predeclared). Two bddo:hasNamespaceBinding entries of one tree document bind the prefix '{?px}'; a prefix is bound at most once."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreePrefixBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:TreeDocument; subjects using bddo:hasNamespaceBinding Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreePrefixBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tree Prefix Binding Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreePrefixBindingShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeSyntax> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Which tree grammar a TreeDocument is written in, and therefore how its nodePath values are read."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TreeSyntax> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Assert this class on a resource representing the defined entity."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TypeSelectionExclusivityShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Type Selection Exclusivity. A bddo:Field must not declare both hasDispatchTable and hasConditionalDataType."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TypeSelectionExclusivityShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TypeSelectionExclusivityShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Type Selection Exclusivity Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#TypeSelectionExclusivityShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VariableLengthFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Variable Length Field. A bddo:bytes or bddo:string field must declare a sizing or termination mechanism."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VariableLengthFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VariableLengthFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Variable Length Field Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VariableLengthFieldShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VarintWidthShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A reusable validation contract for Varint Width. A variable-length integer field (bddo:varuint, bddo:varint, bddo:sqliteVarint) must not declare a width or terminator: its length is discovered from the bytes."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VarintWidthShape> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Validation activation: instances of bddo:Field Constraints apply only within that activation or through shape references; they are not global OWL domain axioms."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VarintWidthShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Varint Width Shape"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#VarintWidthShape> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Namespace prefix declarations reused by SHACL SPARQL constraints and rules. This is validation infrastructure, not a property of parsed data."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Used by named SHACL SPARQL constraints/rules in this module. Not intended for instance-data assertions."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "prefixes"@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#_prefixes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#adler32> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The Adler-32 checksum identifier, producing a 32-bit integrity value for a byte sequence."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#adler32> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#adler32> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#alignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A positive byte-boundary requirement applied when positioning a field under the processing model."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#alignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#alignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The datatype or structure selected when an arm's key matches."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armDataType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The string or integer key value an arm matches by equality."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armKey> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armKey> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The dispatch table an arm contributes to."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armTable> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#armTable> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ascii> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "US-ASCII character encoding using seven-bit character values."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ascii> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#ascii> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiDecimal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A fixed- or floating-point number written as text, occupying the field's declared width or ending at its terminator. Accepts leading sign, decimal point and an exponent introduced by E, e, D or d -- Fortran writes a double-precision exponent with D, and formats written by Fortran (USGSDEM record A) use it. A value spelled 'nan' (any case, optional leading sign) reads as a not-a-number; an infinite value is not accepted. Yields a HEL Float."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiDecimal> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiDecimal> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An integer written as text, occupying the field's declared width (bddo:size) or ending at its terminator. Surrounding space and a leading '+'/'-' are accepted. Radix is bddo:numericBase, default 10. Yields a HEL Integer."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#asciiInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The fixed byte displacement locating a field relative to the selected offset base."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffset> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A HEL expression computing a byte displacement relative to the selected offset base."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The field whose parsed value supplies the byte displacement relative to the selected offset base."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#atOffsetFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseBytes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Primitive category for an uninterpreted byte sequence."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseBytes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseBytes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseFloat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Primitive category for floating-point numeric values, before a particular width is selected."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseFloat> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseFloat> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Primitive category for integral numeric values, before width and signedness are applied."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseInteger> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseString> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Primitive category for textual values interpreted using a character encoding."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseString> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseString> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The primitive interpretation category from which a datatype is constructed."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#baseType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The number of bits occupied by a bit-level field, distinct from a primitive datatype's declared bit width."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitLength> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The order used to consume bits within each byte when reading sub-byte fields; it is independent of the byte order of a multi-byte value."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitOrder> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The fixed number of bits used to represent one value of a primitive datatype."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bitWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bytes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Variable-length primitive byte-sequence datatype; its extent is supplied by the field's sizing mechanism."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bytes> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#bytes> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The integrity-check declaration associated with a field, including its algorithm and covered byte interval."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksum> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksum> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksumAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The algorithm used to compute the integrity value over the declared coverage interval."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksumAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#checksumAlgorithm> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#commentPrefix> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A record beginning with this string (after optional whitespace) is ignored."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#commentPrefix> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#commentPrefix> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The HEL boolean expression that determines whether a conditional type or byte-order rule applies."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#condition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deprecated: a single expression yielding the whole [start,end) range. Superseded by the coversFromExpression/coversToExpression pair, which states each bound separately and so can mix field and expression ends. Retained for descriptions written against earlier BDDO."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "HEL expression evaluating to the covered range's START byte offset, inclusive. Alternative to coversFromField for the same bound."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The field whose first byte is the inclusive start of a checksum's covered interval."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversFromField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "HEL expression evaluating to the covered range's END byte offset, EXCLUSIVE (one past the last covered byte). Alternative to coversToField for the same bound -- note coversToField names a field whose last byte is included, so the two forms do not take the same number."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToExpression> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The field whose last byte is included in a checksum's covered interval. This differs from the exclusive end used by coversToExpression."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToField> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#coversToField> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/CCITT-FALSE integrity check: polynomial 0x1021, initial value 0xFFFF, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x0000 (check value 0x29B1 over the ASCII bytes 123456789). Other CRC-16 variants, such as CRC-16/ARC or CRC-16/XMODEM, have identifiers of their own."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Arc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/ARC integrity check: width 16, polynomial 0x8005, initial value 0x0000, input and output reflected and final XOR 0x0000 (check value 0xBB3D over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Arc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Arc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Modbus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/MODBUS integrity check: width 16, polynomial 0x8005, initial value 0xFFFF, input and output reflected and final XOR 0x0000 (check value 0x4B37 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Modbus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Modbus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16X25> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/IBM-SDLC (X-25) integrity check: width 16, polynomial 0x1021, initial value 0xFFFF, input and output reflected and final XOR 0xFFFF (check value 0x906E over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16X25> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16X25> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Xmodem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-16/XMODEM integrity check: width 16, polynomial 0x1021, initial value 0x0000, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x0000 (check value 0x31C3 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Xmodem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc16Xmodem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-32/ISO-HDLC integrity check used by zlib and PNG: reflected polynomial 0xEDB88320, initial value 0xFFFFFFFF and final XOR 0xFFFFFFFF (check value 0xCBF43926 over the ASCII bytes 123456789). Other 32-bit CRC variants, such as CRC-32C, have identifiers of their own."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Bzip2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-32/BZIP2 integrity check: width 32, polynomial 0x04C11DB7, initial value 0xFFFFFFFF, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0xFFFFFFFF (check value 0xFC891918 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Bzip2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Bzip2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Mpeg2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-32/MPEG-2 integrity check: width 32, polynomial 0x04C11DB7, initial value 0xFFFFFFFF, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x00000000 (check value 0x0376E6E7 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Mpeg2> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32Mpeg2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32c> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-32/ISCSI (CRC-32C) integrity check: width 32, polynomial 0x1EDC6F41, initial value 0xFFFFFFFF, input and output reflected and final XOR 0xFFFFFFFF (check value 0xE3069283 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32c> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc32c> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Ecma182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-64/ECMA-182 integrity check: width 64, polynomial 0x42F0E1EBA9EA3693, initial value 0x0000000000000000, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x0000000000000000 (check value 0x6C40DF5F0B497347 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Ecma182> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Ecma182> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Xz> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-64/XZ integrity check: width 64, polynomial 0x42F0E1EBA9EA3693, initial value 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, input and output reflected and final XOR 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (check value 0x995DC9BBDF1939FA over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Xz> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc64Xz> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc8Smbus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC-8/SMBUS integrity check: width 8, polynomial 0x07, initial value 0x00, no input or output reflection and final XOR 0x00 (check value 0xF4 over the ASCII bytes 123456789)."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc8Smbus> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crc8Smbus> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcCheck> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The CRC of the nine ASCII bytes \"123456789\" under the algorithm's parameters: the catalogue check value that identifies a CRC variant. Informative on a named algorithm; never required, and never read by a processor."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcCheck> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcInit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The value the CRC register holds before the first byte is processed, unreflected, below 2^width."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcInit> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcPolynomial> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The generator polynomial of a CRC without its top (x^width) term, in normal (unreflected) form, as a non-negative integer below 2^width: CRC-32's is 0x04C11DB7 (79764919), not the reflected 0xEDB88320."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcPolynomial> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcReflectIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If true, each input byte is processed least-significant bit first (reflected); if false, most-significant bit first."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcReflectIn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcReflectOut> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If true, the final register is bit-reversed over its width before the final XOR."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcReflectOut> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The width of a CRC in bits, 8 to 64: the degree of its generator polynomial and the width of its register and result."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcWidth> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcXorOut> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The value XORed into the (possibly reflected) final register to give the CRC, below 2^width."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#crcXorOut> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#currentPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Offset reference at the parser's current position before the explicitly addressed field is read."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#currentPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use this IRI as a controlled value where the profile or a shape accepts its declared type."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#currentPosition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo> .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#dataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The primitive datatype or nested structure used to interpret a physical field when a conditional type does not replace it."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#dataType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
