<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#enumIsFlags> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "If true, the Enumeration is a bit-flag set: each EnumValue's raw value is a bitmask, and every symbol whose bit(s) are set in the parsed value is emitted."@en .
<https://hexplain.io/ns/bddo#enumIsFlags> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Use in physical binary-format descriptions. Extents and offsets describe bytes unless a term explicitly specifies bits; HEL evaluation and failure behavior follow the processing specification. Use it as a predicate. Applicable SHACL paths and their focus-node scopes are listed below; no additional global domain is inferred from that usage."@en .
